From fb606fcc3b4359b99e3c3b3293ce81f0700b0de0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 05:59:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] internet_speed: reset the retry budget on every run

level_err_cnt is reset on success, on tripping LEVEL_ERR_MAX and on the silent
retry path - but NOT when a run fails with its budget already spent. The
counter therefore leaked across runs within one session, so a later test could
start with no retries left and abort partway through on the first transient
error. It got worse the longer the tab stayed open, which is exactly how it was
reported.

Reset it per run alongside the other per-run state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/internet_speed.html | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/internet_speed.html b/release/src/router/www/internet_speed.html
index 9d8bc086da..2e053cdea3 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/internet_speed.html
+++ b/release/src/router/www/internet_speed.html
@@ -383,6 +383,12 @@ function reset_speedTest_div(){
 function start_speedTest(){
 	speedTest_retry_done = false;	/* reaper: fresh retry budget per user-initiated run */
 	speedTest_poll_inflight = false;	/* reaper: clear any stale in-flight poll guard */
+	level_err_cnt = 0;	/* reaper: per-run too. It is reset on success, on tripping
+			   LEVEL_ERR_MAX, and on the silent-retry path - but NOT when a run fails
+			   with its retry budget already spent, so the count leaked into the next
+			   run and later tests in a session aborted early on errors the earlier
+			   ones had accumulated. A page reload hid it, which is why it read as
+			   random. */
 	reset_speedTest_div();
 	change_speedTestBtn("testing");
 	if(!enable_auto_server && cur_server_id != "")
-- 
